---
// /benchmark/: how well each model does the tracker's own research job, measured on real pages
// with known answers (benchmark/README.md). One row a model and variant, pooled over its runs; each
// opens its own page with the runs side by side (model.astro).
import Base from "../../src/layouts/Base.astro";
import "./benchmark.css";
import Leaderboard from "./Leaderboard.astro";
import Scatter from "./Scatter.astro";
import HeatTable from "./HeatTable.astro";
import CaseMatrix from "./CaseMatrix.astro";
import { runs, cases, sets, FAMILIES, FAMILY_NOTE, CAPABILITIES, day, score, tokens, tip, modelName, subjectLine, rankedVariants, variantRow, usd } from "./data.js";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const { full, partial } = sets();
const current = full[0];
const older = full.slice(1);
const families = Object.keys(FAMILIES);
const weights = runs[0]?.weights ?? { facts: 20, figures: 20, classification: 10, corroboration: 15, photos: 10, text: 15, grounding: 10 };
const byFamily = families.map((family) => [family, cases.filter((item) => item.family === family)]);

const variants = rankedVariants().map((g) => variantRow(g, base));
const priced = variants.filter((row) => row.cost).length;
const unconfirmed = variants.filter((row) => row.cost?.unconfirmed).length;
const dotRows = (row) => [["", "Score", score(row.score)], ["", "Tokens a case", tokens(row.t.total)], ["", "List price a case", row.cost ? usd(row.cost.perCase) : "none"], ["", "Minutes a case", String(row.min ?? "?")], ["", "Runs", row.sub]];
const dots = (x) => variants.map((row) => ({ id: row.id, name: row.name, href: row.href, x: x(row), y: row.score, rows: dotRows(row) }));
// what one result of 85 or more costs at list price: a case's cost over the share that pass
const perPass = variants.filter((row) => row.cost && row.v.pass > 0).map((row) => ({ ...row, share: row.v.pass / row.attempts, usdPass: row.cost.perCase / (row.v.pass / row.attempts) })).sort((a, b) => a.usdPass - b.usdPass);
const maxPass = Math.max(...perPass.map((row) => row.usdPass), 1e-9);
// the cases the models find hardest
const hardest = cases.map((item) => {
  const values = variants.map((row) => row.caseScore(item.id)).filter((value) => value != null);
  return { item, n: values.length, mean: values.length ? values.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / values.length : null, pass: values.filter((value) => value >= 85).length };
}).filter((entry) => entry.mean != null).sort((a, b) => a.mean - b.mean).slice(0, 10);
const top = variants[0];
const fullRuns = current?.runs.length ?? 0;
---
<Base title="Research benchmark" description="How well each AI model does the tracker's research: recognising events, corroborating them, finding photos, getting figures and classification right, and what it costs." wide noindex>
  <div class="bench">
    <h1>Research benchmark</h1>
    <p class="lead">Which model can be trusted with the tracker's research? Each one gets the same {cases.length} real pages
      and does the whole job the way it runs in production: read the page, search for other coverage, check what the
      tracker already has, decide, and write the report. The result is compared with a checked answer.</p>

    <div class="b-kpis">
      <div class="b-kpi"><b>{variants.length}</b><span>Models and variants</span><em>{fullRuns} full runs · {runs.length - fullRuns} unfinished or partial</em></div>
      <div class="b-kpi"><b>{cases.length}</b><span>Cases</span><em>{byFamily.map(([family, list]) => `${list.length} ${FAMILIES[family].toLowerCase()}`).join(" · ")}</em></div>
      <div class="b-kpi"><b>{top ? score(top.score) : "–"}<small> / 100</small></b><span>Best score</span><em>{top ? top.name : "no full run yet"}</em></div>
      <div class="b-kpi"><b>{hardest[0] ? score(hardest[0].mean) : "–"}<small> mean</small></b><span>Hardest case</span><em>{hardest[0]?.item.title ?? ""}</em></div>
    </div>

    {!runs.length && (
      <p class="note">No run has been recorded yet. Start one with <code>npm run benchmark -- opencode@provider/model#effort</code>.</p>
    )}

    {current && (
      <>
        <h2 id="results">Results</h2>
        <p class="note">One row a model with its effort setting. All its full runs count, whatever harness or provider served
          them: a case's score is the mean of all its results, and the model's score the mean over cases. Open a row for its
          runs side by side.</p>

        <Leaderboard title="Score, verdicts and what a case takes" sub={`ranked by score · ${cases.length} cases`} rows={variants}
          note={`Pass is a case score of 85 or more, partial 50 or more. The thin line on a score bar spans the lowest and highest single run or repeat. Tokens are everything read and written for one case, cache included. List price is those tokens at the maker's own API price, the same basis whoever served them (${priced} of ${variants.length} have one; ≈ marks ${unconfirmed} that only third parties report). Point at a figure for its parts.`} />

        <h2 id="efficiency">Cost, speed and score</h2>
        <p class="note">Each dot is one model and variant. Further left is cheaper or faster, higher is better. The dark dots are
          the ones no other model beats with a higher score for less: the sensible choices.</p>
        <div class="b-grid2">
          <Scatter title="Score against list price" sub="list price of one case, at the maker's own rates" kind="usd" axis="list price a case (log scale) → · ↑ score"
            points={dots((row) => row.cost?.perCase)} />
          <Scatter title="Score against time" sub="typical minutes for one case, page to final answer" kind="minutes" axis="minutes a case → · ↑ score"
            points={dots((row) => row.min)} />
          <Scatter title="Score against tokens" sub="everything read and written for one case, cache included" kind="tokens" axis="tokens a case (log scale) → · ↑ score"
            points={dots((row) => row.t.total)} />
          <figure class="b-card" data-chart>
            <figcaption><b>What one passing result costs</b> <span>list price a case ÷ share of cases passed · cheapest first</span></figcaption>
            <ol class="b-hbars">
              {perPass.map((row) => (
                <li>
                  <a class="name" href={row.href}>{row.name}</a>
                  <span class="b-meter" tabindex="0" data-tip={tip(row.name, "one passing result at list price", [["", "List price a case", usd(row.cost.perCase)], ["", "Cases passed", `${Math.round(row.share * 100)}%`], ["", "A passing result", usd(row.usdPass)], ["", "Minutes a passing result", row.min ? String(Math.round((row.min / row.share) * 10) / 10) : "?"]])}>
                    <span class="track"><i style={`width:${(row.usdPass / maxPass) * 100}%`}></i></span><b>{row.cost.unconfirmed ? "≈" : ""}{usd(row.usdPass)}</b>
                  </span>
                  <span class="of">{Math.round(row.share * 100)}% pass</span>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ol>
            <p class="chart-note">A cheap model that often fails can cost more per usable report than a dearer one that passes. Free previews without a list price are left out.</p>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <figure class="b-card" data-chart>
          <figcaption><b>The hardest cases</b> <span>mean score over the {variants.length} models and variants, lowest first</span></figcaption>
          <ol class="b-hbars">
            {hardest.map((entry) => (
              <li>
                <a class="name" href={`#case-${entry.item.id}`} title={entry.item.title}>{entry.item.title}<small>{FAMILIES[entry.item.family].toLowerCase()}</small></a>
                <span class="b-meter" tabindex="0" data-tip={tip(entry.item.title, FAMILIES[entry.item.family], [["", "Mean score", score(entry.mean)], ["", "Models that pass", `${entry.pass} of ${entry.n}`]])}>
                  <span class="track"><i style={`width:${entry.mean}%`}></i></span><b>{score(entry.mean)}</b>
                </span>
                <span class="of">{entry.pass} of {entry.n} pass</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
          <p class="chart-note">These are the cases that tell the models apart. A case every model passes says little.</p>
        </figure>

        <HeatTable title="Where each model loses points" sub="scores by kind of case and by part of the report · the stronger the wash, the more was lost" rows={variants} />

        <h2 id="cases">Case by case</h2>
        <p class="note">One row a case, one column a model and variant, in ranked order. Each cell is the mean of its results on
          that case and opens the model's page there.</p>
        <CaseMatrix columns={variants} />
      </>
    )}

    {(older.length > 0 || partial.length > 0) && (
      <>
        <h2 id="other">Unfinished and partial runs</h2>
        <p class="note">Runs that stopped before the end, runs of only some cases, and runs on an earlier set of cases, other
          run settings or older scoring rules. They are kept for reference and do not count in the results above.</p>
        <div class="b-scroll">
          <table class="b-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Model</th><th class="n">Score so far</th><th class="n">Cases</th><th>Why apart</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {[...older.flatMap((set) => set.runs.map((run) => [run, "earlier cases, settings or rules"])), ...partial.map((run) => [run, run.complete ? "only some cases" : "stopped before the end"])].map(([run, reason]) => (
                <tr>
                  <td><span class="b-model"><a href={`${base}benchmark/${run.id}/`}>{modelName(run)}</a></span><span class="b-sub">{subjectLine(run)} · {day(run.started_at)}</span></td>
                  <td class="n">{score(run.summary.score)}</td>
                  <td class="n">{run.summary.cases} of {cases.length}</td>
                  <td>{reason}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </>
    )}

    <h2 id="how">How it works</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>A run starts a private copy of the tracker's own research service, the same program and the same instructions
        that research submissions in production, with the model under test. It works against a copy of the reports in
        which the answers to the cases have been taken out. Each case's page is submitted like any link a reader sends.
        Nothing is published: the copy is thrown away after the run. The live tracker already shows the hidden
        answers, so in the copy the model is told that the tracker's own site is never a source; an answer that
        names a hidden report anyway is marked spoiled and not counted.</p>
      <p>What the service ends with is then compared, by fixed rules and without a judging model, with an answer that was
        checked by hand against the sources.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Three kinds of case</h3>
    <div class="b-scroll">
      <table class="b-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th class="n">Cases</th><th>What is asked</th><th>How it is scored</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>{FAMILIES["new-event"]}</td><td class="n">{byFamily[0][1].length}</td><td>{FAMILY_NOTE["new-event"]}</td><td>No report: 0. Otherwise the report is scored part by part (below).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>{FAMILIES["known-event"]}</td><td class="n">{byFamily[1][1].length}</td><td>{FAMILY_NOTE["known-event"]}</td><td>100 when it is attached to the right report or called its duplicate; 0 for a second report or the wrong one.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>{FAMILIES["out-of-scope"]}</td><td class="n">{byFamily[2][1].length}</td><td>{FAMILY_NOTE["out-of-scope"]}</td><td>100 for the right decision, part credit for another rejection, 0 for a report.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>Inside a report</h3>
    <div class="b-scroll">
      <table class="b-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Part</th><th class="n">Weight</th><th>What is checked</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {Object.keys(weights).map((key) => <tr><td>{CAPABILITIES[key][0]}</td><td class="n">{weights[key]}</td><td>{CAPABILITIES[key][1]}</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>A part that a case cannot test is left out for that case: a story only one outlet carried has no corroboration
        score. Many cases hold a trap that halves the figures score when it is walked into, such as pounds recorded as
        kilograms or cocaine added to the cannabis weight.</p>
      <p>The overall score is the mean over all cases. Models differ from run to run, so a difference of a few points
        between two rows means little; repeat a run (<code>--repeat 3</code>) to see how much one model varies.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Tokens and cost</h3>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Every run records the tokens the harness reports for each case: fresh input, input read from the provider's
        cache, output and reasoning. Tokens a case is their sum over the whole run divided by the cases run, so a model
        that needs many steps, reads many pages or repeats itself shows it here.</p>
      <p>List price a case is those tokens at the maker's own API price, each kind at its own rate (cached input is far
        cheaper than fresh), the same basis whoever served the model and whatever plan paid for it. Where the provider's
        own price, a subscription's share or the harness's own figure is known, pointing at the price shows it too.
        Free previews whose maker publishes no price show a dash. The prices are kept with their sources in
        <code>src/lib/models.js</code>, which the tracker also uses for its own research runs.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Running it</h3>
    <pre><code>npm run benchmark -- opencode@swancloud/muse-spark-1.3-contributor#xhigh
npm run benchmark -- muse@muse-spark-1.3#xhigh --repeat 3
npm run benchmark:scores</code></pre>
    <p class="note">The cases, the scoring rules and every run's full output are in the repository's <code>benchmark/</code> folder.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
<script>
  import "../../src/scripts/chart-tooltip.js";
</script>
